That's a good project. A **coffee shop landing page** is realistic, lets you practice design, and covers many of the skills you'll use on larger websites.

Here's what you could include.

## 1. Navigation Bar

At the top of the page:

* Coffee shop logo
* Home
* Menu
* About
* Testimonials
* Contact
* "Order Now" button

---done

## 2. Hero Section

This is the first thing visitors see.

Include:

* A large coffee image
* Catchy headline
* Short description
* Two buttons:

  * ☕ Order Now
  * 📖 View Menu

Example text:

> Freshly Brewed Coffee Every Morning
>
> Crafted with premium beans and served with passion.

---done

## 3. Featured Drinks

Display your most popular drinks in cards.

Example:

| Image | Coffee     | Price |
| ----- | ---------- | ----- |
| ☕     | Espresso   | $3.50 |
| ☕     | Cappuccino | $4.50 |
| ☕     | Latte      | $5.00 |
| ☕     | Mocha      | $5.50 |

Each card can have:

* Image
* Name
* Description
* Price
* Order button

---done

## 4. About Us

Tell visitors about the coffee shop.

Example:

> We have been serving handcrafted coffee since 2015. Every cup is made from carefully selected beans sourced from trusted farmers around the world.

---done

## 5. Why Choose Us

Use icons with short descriptions.

Example:

* 🌱 Premium Beans
* 👨‍🍳 Expert Baristas
🍰 Homemade pastries
🌱 Organic ingredients
❤️ Friendly service

